{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user asked me to build the complete cinema seat-booking web application described in `spec/README.md`, implemented as the existing Angular application `cinescope` (Nx project in `apps/cinescope`) in this Nx workspace. The technology stack is described in `spec/stack.md`. The work is explicitly split into ordered tickets under `spec/tickets/` (01 through 07) which must be implemented in order. `spec/README.md` is stated to be the **complete** specification — I was told explicitly not to ask any clarifying questions, and wherever the spec is silent I should choose the simplest option that satisfies it. The task is only finished when **every ticket is done** AND `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds. This was the only message from the user in the entire conversation; all subsequent conversation content has been my own tool-driven research, implementation, and verification work, plus system-generated tool results and task notifications (none of which constitute user confirmation or approval of anything).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Nx 23 monorepo, Angular 22 standalone zoneless application, SCSS, Vitest, ESLint (angular-eslint flat config, `app` prefix/camelCase directive & kebab-case component selectors enforced).\n   - Angular Material 22 + CDK (buttons, checkbox, datepicker, form-field/input, snack-bar) — UI library must be used for every button, text field, checkbox, toast, and the datepicker; the seat map/legend/selected-seats panel must be custom-drawn by the app.\n   - `@angular/animations` package is **NOT installed** in this workspace — any import from `@angular/platform-browser/animations` or `/animations/async` breaks the production build (`Could not resolve \"@angular/animations/browser\"`). The app must run Angular Material components with **no animations provider configured at all**.\n   - json-server backend (`pnpm api`, port 3000) serving `db.json` (movies, screenings with `occupiedSeats`, reservations) — read-only except `POST /reservations`.\n   - Angular Router with route guards (`CanActivateFn`) enforcing the booking lifecycle rules (section 3.1 of spec).\n   - `sessionStorage`-backed booking state exposed via Angular **signals** (not RxJS state/Reactive Forms) for zoneless-compatible reactivity.\n   - CSS Grid-based auditorium rendering with a fixed 28-track column template per row to guarantee global column alignment (AC-08) across rows with different seat/entrance/couch content.\n   - Signal-based form validation approach in checkout (custom field-level signals + computed error messages + manual touched-tracking) chosen specifically to avoid ambiguity around Reactive Forms + zoneless change detection interaction.\n   - `data-testid` / `data-*` attribute contract (section 9) is extremely strict — exact names, no renaming/abbreviating, specific elements only.\n   - pnpm package manager; `CI=true` environment variable required to avoid an interactive TTY prompt that aborts `pnpm nx build`/`pnpm install` reinstall step in this sandboxed environment.\n   - Need for real browser-driven verification: no `chromium-cli` tool available in this environment; no `playwright`/`puppeteer` npm packages installed locally; however a Playwright-managed Chromium binary already exists on disk at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome`, and `npx --yes playwright <cmd>` is usable to fetch the CLI package on demand.\n   - Tight USD budget constraint for this session (budget started at $5; roughly $1.75 remained at the last checkpoint) — must work efficiently, avoid costly operations, and prefer direct code writing over expensive subagent delegation.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Modified (pre-existing scaffold files):**\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/app.config.ts` — final content:\n     ```ts\n     import { ApplicationConfig, provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners } from '@angular/core';\n     import { provideHttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';\n     import { provideNativeDateAdapter } from '@angular/material/core';\n     import { provideRouter } from '@angular/router';\n     import { appRoutes } from './app.routes';\n\n     export const appConfig: ApplicationConfig = {\n       providers: [provideBrowserGlobalErrorListeners(), provideRouter(appRoutes), provideNativeDateAdapter(), provideHttpClient()],\n     };\n     ```\n     (Animations providers were tried and removed — see Errors section.)\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/app.routes.ts` — final content:\n     ```ts\n     import { Route } from '@angular/router';\n     import { bookingInProgressGuard, bookingPaidGuard } from './core/booking.guards';\n     import { CheckoutComponent } from './pages/checkout/checkout.component';\n     import { ConfirmationComponent } from './pages/confirmation/confirmation.component';\n     import { MovieListComponent } from './pages/movie-list/movie-list.component';\n     import { SeatSelectionComponent } from './pages/seat-selection/seat-selection.component';\n     import { SummaryComponent } from './pages/summary/summary.component';\n\n     export const appRoutes: Route[] = [\n       { path: '', component: MovieListComponent },\n       { path: 'screenings/:id/seats', component: SeatSelectionComponent },\n       { path: 'screenings/:id/summary', component: SummaryComponent, canActivate: [bookingInProgressGuard] },\n       { path: 'screenings/:id/checkout', component: CheckoutComponent, canActivate: [bookingInProgressGuard] },\n       { path: 'confirmation', component: ConfirmationComponent, canActivate: [bookingPaidGuard] },\n       { path: '**', redirectTo: '' },\n     ];\n     ```\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/app.ts` / `app.html` — left unmodified (still just `<router-outlet />`); no changes needed since MatSnackBar manages its own overlay for toasts.\n\n   **New files created (core/services):**\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/models.ts` — `Movie`, `Screening`, `ReservationCustomer`, `CreateReservationPayload`, `Reservation` interfaces, matching section 2.1 exactly (`format: 'PL dubbing' | 'PL subtitles'`).\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/booking.model.ts` — `CheckoutFormValues` (firstName, lastName, email, confirmEmail, phone, termsAccepted), `Booking` interface (screeningId, seats: string[], form, paid, customerEmail), `emptyForm()` factory function.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/api.service.ts` — `ApiService` injectable, `BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000'`, methods `getMovies()`, `getMovie(id)`, `getScreeningsByDate(date)` (uses `HttpParams`), `getScreening(id)`, `createReservation(payload)`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/booking.service.ts` — `BookingService`, `STORAGE_KEY = 'cinescope.booking'`, signal-backed with `readFromStorage()`/`persist()` private helpers; public API: `booking` (readonly signal), `ensureBookingFor(screeningId)`, `isActiveFor(screeningId)`, `isPaid()`, `toggleSeats(ids): 'added'|'removed'|'limit'` (atomic pair toggling for couches, enforces 10-seat cap via `current.seats.length + ids.length > 10`), `removeSeats(ids)`, `updateForm(values)`, `markPaid(email)`, `clear()`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/booking.guards.ts`:\n     ```ts\n     export const bookingInProgressGuard: CanActivateFn = (route) => {\n       const bookingService = inject(BookingService);\n       const router = inject(Router);\n       const id = Number(route.paramMap.get('id'));\n       return bookingService.isActiveFor(id) || router.parseUrl('/');\n     };\n\n     export const bookingPaidGuard: CanActivateFn = () => {\n       const bookingService = inject(BookingService);\n       const router = inject(Router);\n       return bookingService.isPaid() || router.parseUrl('/');\n     };\n     ```\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/core/toast.service.ts` — `ToastService` wrapping `MatSnackBar`, `show(message)` dismisses any existing ref then calls `openFromComponent(ToastComponent, { data: { message }, duration: 4000, horizontalPosition: 'center', verticalPosition: 'bottom' })`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/shared/toast/toast.component.ts`:\n     ```ts\n     @Component({\n       selector: 'app-toast',\n       template: `<span data-testid=\"toast\">{{ data.message }}</span>`,\n     })\n     export class ToastComponent {\n       protected readonly data = inject<{ message: string }>(MAT_SNACK_BAR_DATA);\n     }\n     ```\n\n   **New files created (shared utilities):**\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/shared/date-utils.ts` — `toIso`, `todayIso`, `parseIsoDate`, `isValidIsoDate` (regex + round-trip check to reject invalid dates like Feb 31), `addDays`, `resolveSelectedDate(dateParam)` (returns today if missing/invalid/before today), `weekdayFull`, `showDate(iso, time)` → `\"<Weekday> <D> <Mon> <HH:mm>\"` using full `WEEKDAYS` array and 3-letter `MONTHS` array.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/shared/seat-utils.ts` — `SeatState` type (`'available'|'selected'|'unavailable'|'accessible'`), `COUCH_PRICE = 89`, `seatId(row, column)` → `\"R<row>C<column>\"`, `parseSeatId(id)` (regex `/^R(\\d+)C(\\d+)$/`), `isAccessible(row, column)` (row 1, columns 10-15), `seatPrice(row)` (≤5→25, ≤10→32, else 39), `formatPrice(amount)` → `\"<amount.toFixed(2)> PLN\"`.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/shared/auditorium.ts` — `SeatCellVm`, `CouchCellVm`, `AuditoriumCell` union, `AuditoriumRow` interfaces; `columnTrack(column)` (1-4→+1, 5-20→+2, 21-24→+3, giving 28 total grid tracks); `cellState(ids, isSeat, row, column, occupied, selected)`; `buildAuditorium(occupied, selected)` builds all 15 rows — row 15 generates 12 couch cells (pairs from 1-2 to 23-24), rows 1-10 generate seat cells only for columns 5-20 and 21-24 (no entrance columns 1-4), rows 11-14 generate seat cells for columns 1-24.\n   - `apps/cinescope/src/app/shared/grouping.ts` — `groupColumnsByRow(ids)` helper; `SelectedRowLine` interface + `buildSelectedRowLines(selectedIds)` (sorted rows, row 15 columns paired into `\"a-b\"` strings joined by `, `, other rows joined by `, `); `SummaryItem` interface (`ids`, `row`, `column`, `seatLabel`, `price`) + `buildSummaryItems(selectedIds)` (row 15 → `\"Couch <a>-<b>\"` label with `COUCH_PRICE`, other rows → column-number label with `seatPrice(row)`; final sort by row then column); `pairColumns(columns)` helper.\n\n   **New files created (pages/seat-selection):**\n   - `seat-row.component.ts` — `SeatRowComponent`, `row = input.required<AuditoriumRow>()`, **`seatToggle = output<string[]>()`** (renamed from `toggle` due to an `@angular-eslint/no-output-native` lint error — see Errors section), `cellKey(cell)`, `onCellClick(cell)` (ignores clicks on `state === 'unavailable'`, emits one id for a seat or two ids for a couch via `seatId()`).\n   - `seat-row.component.html` — renders `.seat-row` div (`data-testid=\"seat-row\"`, `[attr.data-row]`), `row-label-left`/`row-label-right` at grid columns 1/28, two `.aisle` divs at grid columns 6/23, and a `@for` loop over `row().cells` rendering either a `seat` button (`data-testid=\"seat\"`, `data-row`, `data-column`, `data-state`, `[style.grid-column]=\"cell.track\"`, text = column number) or a `couch` button (`data-testid=\"couch\"`, `data-row`, `data-column-start`, `data-column-end`, `data-state`, `[style.grid-column]=\"cell.track + ' / span 2'\"`, text = `\"<start>-<end>\"`).\n   - `seat-row.component.scss` — `grid-template-columns: 2rem repeat(4, 2.2rem) 4.4rem repeat(16, 2.2rem) 4.4rem repeat(4, 2.2rem) 2rem;` plus `.state-available/.state-selected/.state-unavailable/.state-accessible` classes using the exact spec hex colors (#2E7D32/#F9A825/#C62828/#1565C0), no hover/focus background overrides (per spec requirement that hover/focus must not change background).\n   - `seat-selection.component.ts` — `SeatSelectionComponent` (imports `MatButtonModule`, `SeatRowComponent`); loads the screening reactively via `route.paramMap` subscription + `ApiService.getScreening(id)`, on error `router.navigateByUrl('/')`, on success `screening.set(...)` + `bookingService.ensureBookingFor(screening.id)`; computed `subtitle` (via `showDate`), `selectedIds`/`selectedCount`/`selectedRowLines` (via `buildSelectedRowLines`), `rows` (via `buildAuditorium`); static `legendItems` array (`available/selected/unavailable/accessible` with labels); `onToggle(ids)` calls `bookingService.toggleSeats(ids)` and shows the `'Maximum 10 seats per booking'` toast on `'limit'`; `cancel()` clears booking + navigates to `/`; `continueToSummary()` guards on empty selection, else navigates to `/screenings/:id/summary`.\n   - `seat-selection.component.html` — title (`seat-map-title`), subtitle (`seat-map-subtitle`), `seat-limit-info` paragraph, `screen-indicator` div, `seat-map` container looping `<app-seat-row [row]=\"row\" (seatToggle)=\"onToggle($event)\" />`, `legend` with `legend-item` loop, `selected-seats` panel (`selected-seats-count`, `selected-seats-row` loop), and `cancel-button`/`continue-button` (disabled when `selectedCount() === 0`).\n   - `seat-selection.component.scss` — layout/legend swatch styles (hex values duplicated intentionally rather than shared via Sass `@use`, to keep each component's styles independently encapsulated — deliberate simplicity choice).\n\n   **New files created (pages/movie-list):**\n   - `movie-list.component.ts` — `MovieListComponent` (imports `MatButtonModule`, `MatDatepickerModule`, `MatFormFieldModule`, `MatInputModule`); `minDate` (today at local midnight); `dayButtons` computed once via IIFE in field initializer (`Today` + next 4 weekdays via `addDays`/`weekdayFull`); `selectedDate` signal driven by `route.queryParamMap` subscription via `resolveSelectedDate(params.get('date'))`, triggering `loadMovies()` on each change; `datepickerValue` computed (`null` if `selectedDate` matches a day button, else a `Date`); `loading`/`error`/`movies`/`screenings` signals; `movieCards` computed (filters movies with ≥1 screening that day, screenings sorted by `time.localeCompare`); `loadMovies()` using `forkJoin({ movies: ..., screenings: ... })`; `selectDay(date)` does `router.navigate([], { relativeTo: this.route, queryParams: { date } })`; `onDatepickerChange(date)` converts to ISO and calls `selectDay`; `openScreening(screeningId)` navigates to seats route.\n   - `movie-list.component.html` — `day-picker` container with `day-button` loop (`data-date`, `data-selected`) plus a `mat-form-field` (`data-testid=\"date-picker\"`) wrapping a `matDatepicker` input with `[min]=\"minDate\"`; then `@if/@else if` chain for `movies-loading` / `movies-error` + `movies-retry-button` / `movies-empty` / `movie-list` with `movie-card` loop (`movie-title`, `movie-genre`, `movie-runtime` = `\"<n> min\"`, `movie-format`, `screening-button` loop labelled with `screening.time`).\n   - `movie-list.component.scss` — basic flex layout.\n\n   **New files created (pages/summary):**\n   - `summary.component.ts` — `SummaryComponent`; `screeningId` from `route.snapshot.paramMap`; `screening`/`movie` signals populated via `api.getScreening(id).pipe(switchMap(screening => api.getMovie(screening.movieId).pipe(map(movie => ({screening, movie})))))`, redirecting to `/` on error; `items`/`total` computed via `buildSummaryItems`/price sum; `formatPrice` re-exported for template use; `remove(item)` calls `bookingService.removeSeats(item.ids)` then navigates to seats route if the booking becomes empty; `back()`/`confirm()` simple navigations.\n   - `summary.component.html` — `summary-title`, `summary-list` with `summary-item` divs (`summary-item-title`, `summary-item-datetime` = `\"<date> <time>\"`, `summary-item-row`, `summary-item-seat`, `summary-item-price`, `summary-item-remove-button`), `summary-total` = `\"Total: <formatPrice(total())>\"`, `back-button`/`confirm-button`.\n   - `summary.component.scss`.\n\n   **New files created (pages/checkout):**\n   - `checkout.component.ts` — `CheckoutComponent` (imports `MatButtonModule`, `MatCheckboxModule`, `MatFormFieldModule`, `MatInputModule`); `screeningId` from route snapshot; `initialForm` read once from `bookingService.booking()?.form ?? emptyForm()`; per-field signals `firstName/lastName/email/confirmEmail/phone/termsAccepted` seeded from `initialForm`; `touched` record signal (all false initially); `submitting` signal; `items`/`total` computed via `buildSummaryItems`; computed error signals:\n     ```ts\n     protected readonly firstNameError = computed(() => requiredMinLength(this.firstName(), 'First name', 2));\n     protected readonly lastNameError = computed(() => requiredMinLength(this.lastName(), 'Last name', 2));\n     protected readonly emailError = computed(() => {\n       const value = this.email();\n       if (!value) return 'Email is required';\n       return EMAIL_RE.test(value) ? null : 'Enter a valid email address';\n     });\n     protected readonly confirmEmailError = computed(() => {\n       const value = this.confirmEmail();\n       if (!value) return 'Confirm email is required';\n       return value === this.email() ? null : 'Email addresses do not match';\n     });\n     protected readonly phoneError = computed(() => {\n       const value = this.phone();\n       if (!value) return null;\n       return /^\\d{9}$/.test(value) ? null : 'Phone number must be exactly 9 digits';\n     });\n     protected readonly termsError = computed(() => (this.termsAccepted() ? null : 'You must accept the terms and conditions'));\n     ```\n     with `EMAIL_RE = /^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/` module-level constant; `formValid` computed (all errors null); constructor registers an `effect()` that calls `bookingService.updateForm({...all 6 current signal values})` on every change (runs immediately too, harmlessly re-persisting initial values); `inputValue(event)` helper casts `event.target` to `HTMLInputElement`; `touch(field)` sets `touched` map; `onTermsChange(event: MatCheckboxChange)` sets `termsAccepted` + touches it; `back()` navigates to summary; `pay()` — if `submitting()` return; if `!formValid()`, mark all fields touched + `toast.show('The form contains errors')` + return (no request sent); else builds `CreateReservationPayload` with `seats: this.items().flatMap(item => item.ids)` (summary order, not insertion order), submits via `api.createReservation`, on success `markPaid(email)` + navigate to `/confirmation`, on error shows `'Payment failed. Please try again.'` toast and resets `submitting`.\n   - `checkout.component.html` — five `.field` divs each with a `mat-form-field` containing a `mat-label` (`data-testid=\"*-label\"`, text ending in ` *` for the 5 required fields, no asterisk for phone) and a native `<input matInput>` (`data-testid=\"*-input\"`, bound via `[value]`/`(input)=\"field.set(inputValue($event))\"`/`(blur)=\"touch('field')\"`), each followed by a conditional `@if (touched().field && fieldError(); as msg)` error div (`data-testid=\"*-error\"`); a `mat-checkbox` (`data-testid=\"terms-checkbox\"`) with `[checked]`/`(change)=\"onTermsChange($event)\"` wrapping a `<span data-testid=\"terms-label\">`; `checkout-back-button`/`pay-button` (text toggles `\"Processing…\"` vs `\"Pay \" + formatPrice(total())`, `[disabled]=\"submitting()\"`).\n   - `checkout.component.scss`.\n\n   **New files created (pages/confirmation):**\n   - `confirmation.component.ts` — `ConfirmationComponent`; `email` computed from `bookingService.booking()?.customerEmail ?? ''`; `continue()` clears booking + navigates to `/`.\n   - `confirmation.component.html`:\n     ```html\n     <h1 data-testid=\"confirmation-heading\">Payment successful</h1>\n     <p data-testid=\"confirmation-message\">Your tickets will be sent shortly to {{ email() }}</p>\n     <button mat-flat-button type=\"button\" data-testid=\"confirmation-continue-button\" (click)=\"continue()\">Continue</button>\n     ```\n   - `confirmation.component.scss`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **`pnpm nx build cinescope` aborted with `ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY`** on first attempt — pnpm wanted to recreate `node_modules` but refused without a TTY. **Fix:** prefixed the command with `CI=true` (e.g. `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope`), which allowed pnpm to proceed non-interactively. This must be used for all subsequent `pnpm nx build`/`lint`/`test` invocations in this sandbox.\n   - **Build failure: `Could not resolve \"@angular/animations/browser\"`** when `app.config.ts` included `provideAnimationsAsync()` from `@angular/platform-browser/animations/async`. Investigated and confirmed `@angular/animations` package is genuinely absent from `node_modules/@angular/` (only `cdk`, `common`, `compiler`, `compiler-cli`, `core`, `forms`, `material`, `platform-browser`, `router` are installed). Tried switching to `provideNoopAnimations()` from `@angular/platform-browser/animations` instead — got the **same class of error** (`@angular/platform-browser/fesm2022/animations.mjs` statically imports `@angular/animations/browser` even for the noop path). **Final fix:** removed all animation-provider imports/calls from `app.config.ts` entirely — no `provideAnimations`/`provideNoopAnimations`/`provideAnimationsAsync` call at all. Build then succeeded (verified bundle output, exit code 0). **This is a hard constraint going forward: never import from `@angular/platform-browser/animations` or `/animations/async` in this codebase.**\n   - **Lint failure: `@angular-eslint/no-output-native` on `seat-row.component.ts:12`** — the `output<string[]>()` was originally named `toggle`, which collides with the native DOM `toggle` event name. **Fix:** renamed the output property to `seatToggle` in `seat-row.component.ts` (both the `readonly seatToggle = output<string[]>();` declaration and the `this.seatToggle.emit(ids);` call), and updated the template binding in `seat-selection.component.html` from `(toggle)=\"onToggle($event)\"` to `(seatToggle)=\"onToggle($event)\"`. Re-ran `CI=true pnpm nx lint cinescope` → `✔ All files pass linting`.\n   - **No user feedback was received correcting my approach** — these were all self-discovered build/lint errors that I fixed without needing user input, since the user's only instruction was the original task description and explicit \"do not ask questions\" directive.\n   - **json-server port confusion during manual testing** — an early backgrounded `(pnpm api > /tmp/api.log 2>&1 &)` subshell left an orphaned json-server process bound only to IPv6 loopback (`::1:3000`); my own `node -e \"fetch('http://localhost:3000/...')\"` test calls failed with `ECONNREFUSED` against `127.0.0.1`/`localhost` resolution, while `http://[::1]:3000/movies` succeeded and returned real data. A subsequent explicit `pnpm api` launch via the Bash tool's `run_in_background: true` then failed with `EADDRINUSE: address already in use ::1:3000`, confirming the orphaned instance was still alive and functional. **I left this orphaned json-server process running** (it serves data correctly) rather than killing it, and did not yet reconcile whether the actual browser (Chrome, via the dev server) will reach it fine over `localhost:3000` (it likely will, since browsers do dual-stack Happy Eyeballs resolution, but this was not yet empirically confirmed before the summary cutoff).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Resolved the zoneless-change-detection-with-forms ambiguity by choosing a fully signal-driven approach for the checkout form instead of Angular Reactive Forms, sidestepping any uncertainty about whether `FormControl.markAsTouched()`/`statusChanges` would reliably trigger view updates without Zone.js.\n   - Resolved couch \"counts as 2 seats\" requirement elegantly by storing both seat identifiers of a selected couch directly in the flat `booking.seats` array, making `seats.length` naturally equal the \"selected seats count\" without any special-casing in counting logic.\n   - Resolved column-alignment-across-rows requirement (AC-08) via a fixed 28-track CSS Grid template shared by every row, with a pure `columnTrack()` mapping function, so entrance gaps (rows 1-10, cols 1-4) simply have no element placed in those tracks rather than needing placeholder elements.\n   - Resolved the \"keep seats in summary order when POSTing\" requirement (spec section 7.2: \"the booked seat identifiers (in summary order...)\") by deriving the POST payload's `seats` array from `buildSummaryItems(...).flatMap(item => item.ids)` rather than from the raw (click-order) `booking.seats` array.\n   - Resolved the missing `@angular/animations` dependency constraint (see Errors) by running the entire app with zero animation providers configured, relying on Angular Material 22's apparent lack of a hard runtime requirement for one (confirmed only at build time so far, not yet at runtime in a real browser).\n   - **Ongoing/unresolved troubleshooting at cutoff:** setting up real interactive browser verification. No `chromium-cli` tool is available in this environment. No `playwright`/`puppeteer` npm package is installed locally or globally, though `npx --yes playwright <command>` works for fetching the CLI on demand, and a compatible Chromium browser binary is already cached on disk at `/opt/ms-playwright/chromium-1234/chrome-linux/chrome`. I had started the backend (`pnpm api`, confirmed reachable via `[::1]:3000` but with unclear `localhost`/`127.0.0.1` reachability from my own Node test environment specifically) and the Angular dev server (`pnpm nx serve cinescope`, backgrounded task id `b7yeikgdv`, confirmed reachable on port 4200 via a polling loop) in preparation for driving a Playwright-based Node script against the real app, but had not yet written or executed that script before the conversation was interrupted for this summary.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the Angular application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n   \n   (This is the only true user-role message in the conversation. All other content — including the `run` skill's returned instructional text, task notifications about background commands, and system reminders — are not user messages and must not be treated as user feedback, confirmation, or approval of any kind.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Complete ticket 07 (\"Final pass\"): walk through the whole flow — movie list, seat map, summary, checkout, confirmation — against the full specification (section 9 identifiers in particular), fixing whatever does not match; confirm every acceptance criterion (AC-01 through AC-69) in section 10 is met; confirm `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds (already verified once, should be re-verified after any further fixes).\n   - Run `pnpm nx test cinescope` (Vitest) to make sure existing/any tests pass — not yet run at all in this session.\n   - Perform actual interactive runtime verification of the booking flow in a real (headless) browser — was in progress via a Playwright-based approach (dev server + backend already started and reachable) but no interaction script had been written/executed yet.\n   - Specifically verify behaviors that are hard to fully confirm by static code review alone: zoneless reactivity of the checkout form's touched/error messages on blur/input; Angular Material components functioning correctly with zero animation providers configured; the exact runtime attribute value produced by `[attr.data-selected]=\"boolExpr\"` (need to confirm it renders the literal strings `\"true\"`/`\"false\"` as required by spec section 9