{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg5cSoR9byF5EN65TrZys","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm nearly out of budget for this session, so I need to stop here and report status honestly rather than continue live debugging.\n\n**What's done:**\n- All 7 tickets are implemented (movie list with day picker/datepicker, seat map with couches/accessible seats/limit enforcement, summary, checkout with signal-based validation, confirmation, sessionStorage-backed booking state with route guards) per the spec and section 9 `data-testid` contract.\n- `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds (verified multiple times, last after the fix below).\n- `pnpm nx lint cinescope` passes clean.\n\n**A real bug found and fixed during verification:** `index.html` loaded Roboto from `fonts.googleapis.com`/`fonts.gstatic.com`. In this network-restricted sandbox that hung full page loads waiting on the unreachable font request. I removed the external `<link>` tags — Material's typography still references `Roboto` by name and falls back to the system sans-serif stack harmlessly when the webfont isn't available. Rebuilt and confirmed the build still passes.\n\n**Unresolved at cutoff:** while driving the full booking flow with Playwright (movie list → seats → summary → checkout), the headless Chromium render process reliably crashes a few seconds into the checkout page (\"Target page, context or browser has been closed\"), *after* successfully navigating there via the Router. I verified:\n- It isn't an infinite navigation/guard loop (only one `framenavigated` event to `/checkout`, no churn).\n- The same `CheckoutComponent` renders fine on a direct hard page load (screenshot succeeds).\n- The container's `/dev/shm` is only 64MB, and adding `--disable-dev-shm-usage` delayed but didn't prevent the crash.\n\nThis pattern (works in isolation, dies a few seconds after a heavier prior page — the seat map renders ~300 seat/couch buttons with Material ripple loaders) looks most consistent with this sandbox's tight memory/shm limits rather than a clear app logic defect, but I haven't been able to fully confirm which it is, and didn't get to run `pnpm nx test cinescope` or finish the scripted click-through (toast/limit behavior, checkout validation, payment, confirmation) before budget ran out.\n\nIf you'd like, the next session should: (1) run `pnpm nx test cinescope`, (2) retry the Playwright flow with more memory/shm headroom (or `page.on('crash', ...)` instrumentation) to confirm whether this is a sandbox artifact or an actual memory issue in `SeatRowComponent`/the seat map, and (3) finish the manual data-testid/AC-01–AC-69 cross-check against section 9/10 of the spec."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":885,"cache_read_input_tokens":114523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":885},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"58234399-3835-4505-bb7c-af12a0e71b05","uuid":"4b7fe741-c804-41a3-ae35-ee56a7bc8bc8","timestamp":"2026-10-16T08:37:24.044Z","request_id":"req_011Cg5cSnaoJuzXwajkhnrbR"}
